From: Xemorph <finn.brandes@outlook.de>
Date: Mon, 2 Mar 2026 13:41:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Silicon/RP1: add an ACPI I2C1 device

Describe the RP1's I2C1 controller in the DSDT alongside the two xHCI
controllers, so an ACPI-booted OS sees the block that the Rp1BusDxe
vendor child already exposes to UEFI.

Ported from Xemorph/edk2-platforms master (commits cea7196 "Silicon/RP1:
Add initial I2C support" and 7fcf8d1 "Change HID & UID"), squashed: the
second commit only corrects the _HID and drops a bogus integer _CID from
the first, so only the end state is carried here.

The upstream branch also added RP1_I2C_SIZE 0x4000 to Rp1.h. That hunk
is dropped: this tree already defines RP1_I2C_SIZE, as 0x1000, from
0001-Rp1BusDxe-register-GEM-and-I2C1-vendor-devices.patch, and 0x1000 is
what the firmware DTB reports for these controllers (rp1 i2c nodes are
reg = <... 0x1000>). 0x4000 is the stride between instances, not the
register window, and would overlap the next controller.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [imported from a third-party fork]
Signed-off-by: Xemorph <finn.brandes@outlook.de>
---
--- a/Silicon/RaspberryPi/RpiSiliconPkg/Include/Rp1.asi
+++ b/Silicon/RaspberryPi/RpiSiliconPkg/Include/Rp1.asi
@@ -58,3 +58,18 @@
     Return (RBUF)
   }
 }
+
+Device (I2C1) {
+  Name (_HID, "ACPI000E")
+  Name (_UID, 0x1)
+
+  Method (_CRS, 0, Serialized) {
+    Name (RBUF, ResourceTemplate () {
+      RP1_QWORDMEMORY_BUF (00)
+      RP1_INTERRUPT_BUF (01)
+    })
+    RP1_QWORDMEMORY_SET (00, RP1_I2C1_BASE, RP1_I2C_SIZE)
+    RP1_INTERRUPT_SET (01)
+    Return (RBUF)
+  }
+}
